{"title":"Field Service Engineer Roadmap","role":"Field Service Engineer","summary":"A Field Service Engineer installs, commissions, troubleshoots, maintains and repairs technical equipment at customer or industrial sites. For an EIE graduate, the strongest pathway combines instrumentation, industrial automation, control systems, electrical/electronics fundamentals, PLC/SCADA, industrial communication and field troubleshooting.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Timeline assumption":"Four-year B.Tech/B.E. beginning in 2026 and graduating around 2030."},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Field Service Engineer is a directly aligned career for Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering (EIE)."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build instrumentation, electronics, PLC, control systems, industrial networking and troubleshooting skills."},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Develop expertise in industrial automation, process instrumentation, commissioning, drives, robotics or service engineering."},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Take ownership of customer sites, commissioning projects, troubleshooting and service teams."},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Move toward service management, automation architecture, reliability engineering or technical customer leadership."}],"sections":[{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Electrical circuits, electronics, mathematics and physics"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Complete electronics/electrical laboratory projects"},{"text":"Analytical thinking"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Sensors, measurements and 